ttp://www.classicbands.com/day/december%2031.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d22\",\"snippet\":\" ... 17, 000 magazines per week15.2 million unique visitors per month Media Kit Billboard June 15, 2016 August 6, 2019\\ncompany: Eldridge Industries\\ncountry: United States\\nbased: New York City\\nissn: 0006-2510\\noclc: 732913734\\n\\nBillboard (stylized in lowercase since 2013) is an American music and entertainment magazine ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_%28magazine%29\"}],\"query\":\"New York magazine sold $100 million 1991\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... The population was a million in 1800 and more than two million by the middle of the nineteenth century.17 The number of new publications for the 1800-60 period in London, for both newspapers and magazines, is large—some 1500 titles. This is very much higher than ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.gale.com/intl/essays/ed-king-british-newspapers-1800-1860\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... Includes contributions published in 6 regional daily & weekly newspapers and in 47 other political and cultural magazines, entertainment magazines and magazines of the German-speaking countries (Germany, Austria, Switzerland, South Tyrol, Liechtenstein and Luxembourg).\\n\\n- International Herald Tribune Historical Archive, 1888-2013 Sold in over 160 countries and read ... \",\"title\":\"https://libguides.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/newspapers/bytitle\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Founded by Herbert Ingram in 1842, The Illustrated London News was the first illustrated weekly news magazine.\\n\\nBritain\\n\\nThe oldest consumer magazine still in print is The Scots Magazine, which was first published in 1739, though multiple changes in ownership and gaps in publication totalling over 90 years ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magazine\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... Monthly Journal/magazine. Publishers: LeCount and Strong. Noted as \\\"first California magazine.\\\" The Old Pioneer Press |\\n\\n| Placer Times | Sacramento | 1849 - 1850. (Placer Times and Transcript), Sacramento. 1849. Weekly. Converted into a daily and moved to San Francisco for publication. First published on June 28, 1852 under the management ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.maritimeheritage.org/news/California-Newspapers-1800s.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 1937, for instance, they owned nearly one in every two national and local daily papers sold in Britain, as well as one in every three Sunday papers that were sold. The combined circulation of all their newspapers amounted to over thirteen million.[46]\\n\\nThe Times of London ... \",\"title\":\"https://brewminate.com/a-history-of-newspaper-publishing-since-the-17th-century/\"}],\"query\":\"weekly magazine founded 1800s sold 100 million\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_670d1a3c90b54c48b41ec842"},{"content":"I found a key clue! Billboard magazine was sold for $100 million in 1987, and it was founded in 1894 (1800s). Let me verify Billboard's founding date and then search for the club.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d22\", \"start\": 0, \"length\": 3000}","name":"read"},"id":"call_56b569ba5af04c0bb0321c7f","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Billboard magazine Latin music club 1970s California seven nights week\", \"Billboard magazine 1894 founded weekly\", \"Latin music club 1970s Billboard article owner sound system\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_6b9100b4d4864aefb712cfd1","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d22\",\"document_chars\":19119,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"474fd85f14d1bfbd6834c60a2a90e1acf1e407b356f046f1a241d1a07a84c218\",\"snapshot\":\"ec091dee7ef2d806b0a7b11072f12cf033b317504fbf8cefdaf26b4330363978\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Billboard (magazine) - Wikipedia\\ndate: 2002-03-19\\n---\\ntitle: Billboard\\nlogo: 220px|class=skin-invert\\nlogo_size: 220px\\nimage_file: Billboard magazine 16 November 2019 issue 125th anniversary.png\\nimage_caption: November 16, 2019, cover featuring Paul McCartney and highlighting the magazine's 125th anniversary\\nfounder: William Donaldson, James Hennegan\\nwebsite: |}}\\npublisher: Penske Media Corporation\\neditor: Hannah Karp\\nprevious_editor: Lee Zhito, Tony Gervino, Bill Werde, Tamara Conniff\\nlanguage: Arabic, English, Korean, Spanish, Portuguese\\nfounded: 1 November 1894 (as Billboard Advertising)\\nfrequency: Weekly\\ncategory: Entertainment\\ntotal_circulation: 17, 000 magazines per week15.2 million unique visitors per month Media Kit Billboard June 15, 2016 August 6, 2019\\ncompany: Eldridge Industries\\ncountry: United States\\nbased: New York City\\nissn: 0006-2510\\noclc: 732913734\\n\\nBillboard (stylized in lowercase since 2013) is an American music and entertainment magazine published weekly by Penske Media Corporation. The magazine provides music charts, news, video, opinion, reviews, events and styles related to the music industry. Its music charts include the Hot 100, the 200, and the Global 200, tracking the most popular albums and songs in various music genres. It also hosts events, owns a publishing firm and operates several television shows.\\n\\nBillboard was founded in 1894 by William Donaldson and James Hennegan as a trade publication for bill posters. Donaldson acquired Hennegan's interest in 1900 for $500. In the early years of the 20th century, it covered the entertainment industry, such as circuses, fairs and burlesque shows, and also created a mail service for travelling entertainers. Billboard began focusing more on the music industry as the jukebox, phonograph and radio became commonplace. Many topics that it covered became the subjects of new magazines, including Amusement Business in 1961 to cover outdoor entertainment, so that Billboard could focus on music. After Donaldson died in 1925, Billboard was inherited by his and Hennegan's children, who retained ownership until selling it to private investors in 1985. The magazine has since been owned by various parties.\\n\\nHistory\\n\\nEarly history\\n\\nThe first issue of Billboard was published in Cincinnati, Ohio, by William Donaldson and James Hennegan on November 1, 1894. Initially it covered the advertising and bill-posting industry and was known as Billboard Advertising. At the time, billboards, posters, and paper advertisements placed in public spaces were the primary means of advertising. Donaldson handled editorial and advertising, while Hennegan, who owned Hennegan Printing Co., managed magazine production. The first issues were just eight pages long. The paper had columns such as The Bill Room Gossip and The Indefatigable and Tireless Industry of the Bill Poster. A department for agricultural fairs was established in 1896. The Billboard Advertising publication was renamed The Billboard in 189\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_56b569ba5af04c0bb0321c7f"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d93\",\"snippet\":\" ... In Latin America, Latin pop had remained the main subgenre. Tropical, reggaeton, moombahton, soca have also been popular genres while pop rock continues to be successful. In December 2016, Billboard magazine named Enrique Iglesias the 14th most successful and top male dance club artist of all time. \\\"Despacito ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010s_in_music\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... Soul, R&B and Latin music became more influential on the OPM sound by the late 1990s.\\n\\nLegacy\\n\\nIn December 1999, Billboard magazine named Mariah Carey as the Artist of the Decade in the United States. In 1999, Selena was named the \\\"top Latin artist of the '90s ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1990s_in_music\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d94\",\"snippet\":\" ... 8 July 1970\\nbirth_place: Los Angeles, California, U.S.\\noccupation: * Musician, * singer, * songwriter, * record producer\\nyears_active: 1988–present\\nawards: Full list\\nspouse: Marissa Ribisi (m. 2004)\\nchildren: 2\\nmother: Bibbe Hansen\\nfather: David Campbell\\nwebsite: beck.com\\nsignature: Beck signature, Billboard Open Letter 2016.png\\nmodule ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beck\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d95\",\"snippet\":\" ... Only one single charted, the aforementioned \\\"Lightning Strikes\\\", which peaked at number 21 on the Billboard Mainstream Rock chart. As with the tour for Night in the Ruts, Aerosmith was unable to book larger venues, and instead had to rely on filling clubs and theaters, which they struggled ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aerosmith\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d96\",\"snippet\":\" ... hop, r&b, rock music including pop punk and shoegaze, country, k-pop and indie music dominated the Billboard Hot 100 charts. At the same time, underground genres like hyperpop, plugg, jersey club, phonk and rage thrived in niche communities.\\n\\nBritish rock magazine Kerrang! wrote that Olivia Rodrigo ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_in_music\"}],\"query\":\"Billboard magazine Latin music club 1970s California seven nights week\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d22\",\"snippet\":\" ... Arabic, English, Korean, Spanish, Portuguese\\nfounded: 1 November 1894 (as Billboard Advertising)\\nfrequency: Weekly\\ncategory: Entertainment\\ntotal_circulation: 17, 000 magazines per week15.2 million unique visitors per month Media Kit Billboard June 15, 2016 August 6, 2019\\ncompany: Eldridge Industries\\ncountry: United States\\nbased: New York City ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_%28magazine%29\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d97\",\"snippet\":\" ... BILLBOARD HITS\\n\\nWHAT IS BILLBOARD?\\n\\nBILLBOARD is an American music industry magazine that has been in publication since 1894. The magazine's original content included broader entertainment industry information including common 19th century entertainments such as concerts, fairs, and circuses, but eventually began focusing on music only once ... \",\"title\":\"https://kaitlinbove.com/what-is-popular-music\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d98\",\"snippet\":\" ... His great sense of rhythm and hard work has awarded him such accolades as drummer of the year by Rolling Stone magazine, and the second best drummer of all time by LA Weekly.\\n\\nVALAIDA SNOW\\n\\nValadia Snow was born in Chattanooga and raised on the road as her ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.visitchattanooga.com/blog/post/famous-chattanooga-musicians/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d99\",\"snippet\":\" ... Annually.\\n* Arbeyter Fraynd (1885–1914)\\n* Commonweal (1885–1894). Monthly, then weekly.\\n* The Quarterly Musical Review (1885–1888). Quarterly.\\n* The Lady (1885–)\\n* Freedom (1886–)\\n* Atalanta (1887–1898). Monthly.\\n* Stories Illustrated (1887–1888); founded by John Francon Williams.\\n* Murray's Magazine. (1887–1891). Monthly.\\n* Our Little Dots. Pretty pictures and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_19th-century_British_periodicals\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d100\",\"snippet\":\" ... C.\\\", as he was nicknamed, sold millions of records and pioneered a weekly musical variety television show. His weekly television shows and seasonal specials were broadcast throughout the world. In the official RCA Records Billboard magazine memorial, his life was summed up in these few words: \\\"50 years ... \",\"title\":\"https://brevardalz.org/alzheimers-info/famous-people-with-dementia/\"}],\"query\":\"Billboard magazine 1894 founded weekly\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d93\",\"snippet\":\" ... In Latin America, Latin pop had remained the main subgenre. Tropical, reggaeton, moombahton, soca have also been popular genres while pop rock continues to be successful. In December 2016, Billboard magazine named Enrique Iglesias the 14th most successful and top male dance club artist of all time. \\\"Despacito ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010s_in_music\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d101\",\"snippet\":\" ... In an unsuccessful attempt to lessen the charges against the club's co-owners, Schrager's lawyer Mitchell Rogovin alleged that Hamilton Jordan, chief of staff to U.S. president Jimmy Carter, had used cocaine in the club's basement. In anticipation of increasing interest in rock music ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Studio_54\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d102\",\"snippet\":\" ... In their eyes, the target wasn't mainstream pop music but black music.\\n\\nDisco didn't perish overnight. Donna Summer's