very year (except 1970) from 1959 to 1963 and 1967 to 1974. In the late 1960s, the Brazilian club began traveling outside Latin America and Europe. Football was becoming a global phenomenon: for example, in the ... \",\"title\":\"https://transatlantic-cultures.org/pt/catalog/pele-et-le-monde\"}],\"query\":\"Bajadera Latin club 1970s\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Oxnard, California, is notorious for its crime and street gangs, but it is also known for producing some of the toughest Latino prizefighters in the sport of boxing. In 1978, the Community Service Organization chapter led a city-wide effort to form La Colonia Youth Boxing Club to ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nps.gov/articles/latinothemesports.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... Legacy and impact\\n\\nIn 2015, Billboard listed Juan Gabriel among their list of the 30 most influential Latino artists in history, citing his \\\"dramatic performance style\\\" and his redefined concept of romantic Latin pop music. The publication noted Gabriel's appeal among several generations of Latino Americans and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Gabriel\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... the US as a slur against people of Latin-American descent\\n\\n- Beso de Negra — in Spanish, this means \\\"kiss from a Black woman\\\"\\n\\nSambo's\\n\\nThe sole remaining location of Sambo's in Santa Barbara, California is changing its name. The restaurant chain once had more than 1 ... \",\"title\":\"https://blog.ongig.com/diversity-and-inclusion/alleged-racist-brands/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Such Latino-owned businesses often shaped the social and political relationships of their owners, who beca